        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.14,
            0.573,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " An electrician has to repair an electric fault on a pole of height 5 m. She needs to reach a point 1.3m below the top of the pole to undertake the repair work (see Fig. 9.5). What should be the length of the ladder that she should use which, when inclined at an angle of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to the horizontal, would enable her to reach the required position? Also, how far from the foot of the pole should she place the foot of the ladder? (You may take "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 3 } } \\; = 1 . 7 3 )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.359,
            0.572,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig. 9.5, the electrician is required to reach the point B on the pole AD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.605,
            0.139,
            0.882,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.605,
                0.139,
                0.882,
                0.426
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_3_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.405,
            0.136,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.404,
            0.57,
            0.422
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{BD} = \\mathrm{AD} - \\mathrm{AB} = (5 - 1.3) \\mathrm{m} = 3.7 \\mathrm{m}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.429,
            0.574,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, BC represents the ladder. We need to find"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.448,
            0.632,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "its length, i.e., the hypotenuse of the right triangle BDC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.474,
            0.722,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, can you think which trigonometic ratio should we consider?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.499,
            0.29,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It should be sin "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.546,
            0.135,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.604,
            0.205,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.529,
            0.662,
            0.634
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{BD}}{\\mathrm{BC}}=\\sin 60^{\\circ} \\text { or } \\frac{3.7}{\\mathrm{BC}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.644,
            0.537,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e., the length of the ladder should be 4.28 m."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.689,
            0.155,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.676,
            0.529,
            0.719
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{DC}}{\\mathrm{BD}} = \\cot 60^{\\circ} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.752,
            0.14,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.735,
            0.625,
            0.779
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_3_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{DC}=\\frac{3.7}{\\sqrt{3}}=2.14\\mathrm{~m}\\left(\\mathrm{appears.}\\right)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.792,
            0.902,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, she should place the foot of the ladder at a distance of 2.14 m from the pole."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
